about 1.5in two-block overview at full text width on page 1 or 2; a half-width rendering would make the four arm labels illegible. Allow about 0.22 body page including caption.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 4,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 4,\n    \"minimum_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n    ],\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"Use the concept-figure workflow downstream, not during strategy generation. Preserve editable draw.io source. Represent widths as design settings, not a sequence of successes; do not draw a causal norm-to-grokking arrow. Regenerate raster output at least 2400px wide, never upscale. Prefer a vector PDF if an authentic vector export is available; otherwise use the high-resolution PNG.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"width_endpoint_comparison\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Compare width-dependent endpoint behavior and controls without pooling horizons or hiding incomplete final coverage.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"grouped_seed_dotplot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"hidden_width\",\n    \"metric\": \"checkpoint evaluation_accuracy at each setting-specific horizon\",\n    \"split_by\": \"short-horizon selection observations versus final observations\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"At 5.5in total width use two side-by-side panels, each with only three width categories and four arm colors. Target about 5.5 by 2.4in and 0.34 body page with caption. Shared y limits, a single four-entry legend, short labels, and raw seed dots avoid unreadable half-width multi-panel figures.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 4,\n    \"minimum_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n    ],\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"Selection data come directly from /best_correct/evaluation_evidence/episodes in paper_data.json; final data from /final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes. Do not substitute aggregate metric sources for raw curves. Use small deterministic seed offsets, not invented measurements; connect only genuinely paired values if clarity permits. Keep missing width-256 and missing third width-128 final cells visibly empty/labeled, never at zero. Note the width-128 norm-arm identity. Export reproducible PDF and 300-DPI PNG; LaTeX must include the PDF.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"figure_id\": \"fit_and_generalization_onsets\",\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"purpose\": \"Show the fit/generalization separation and distinguish measured delayed events, horizon censoring, and unavailable runs.\",\n    \"figure_type\": \"paired_event_time_dotplot\",\n    \"preferred_generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n    \"group_by\": \"hidden_width_with_seed_offsets\",\n    \"metric\": \"sustained training-fit onset and sustained held-out generalization onset in optimizer updates\",\n    \"split_by\": \"short-horizon selection observations versus final observations\",\n    \"preferred_span\": \"full_width\",\n    \"target_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n    \"layout_rationale\": \"Use the single-column full text width of 5.5in, two panels with three width categories and two marker meanings, about 2.3in high and 0.32 body page with caption. Explicitly label differing x ranges, 6000 and 24000 updates. Width/seed offsets and a shared two-marker legend remain legible at 8.5pt; do not add all four arm trajectories to this figure.\",\n    \"allow_progression\": false,\n    \"max_panels\": 2,\n    \"max_panels_per_row\": 2,\n    \"max_categories_per_panel\": 3,\n    \"max_series_per_panel\": 2,\n    \"minimum_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n    ],\n    \"implementation_notes\": \"This is a direct event-time comparison, not a search trajectory. Read event records and check them against curves and the evaluator definition. Training threshold is 0.99, held-out threshold 0.95, each sustained for three 100-update checkpoints; delayed-event criterion is at least 1000 updates between onsets. At the horizon use an arrow only for a recorded censored trajectory, never for a missing run. Do not draw a finite endpoint for unobserved generalization. Export PDF and 300-DPI PNG and include PDF in LaTeX.\"\n  }\n]\nref keys dict_keys(['campaign_results_dir', 'count', 'generated_at', 'queries', 'reference_query_plan', 'references', 'results_dir'])\n.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/openalex_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/s2_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/scripts/scholarly_fetch.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.py\n.codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/claims_grounding.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/references.bib\n/usr/bin/pdflatex\n","exit_code":127,"status":"failed"}}
