s. Float32 CPU full-batch cross-entropy, torch.optim.AdamW(foreach=False), all parameters including biases decayed.', 'initialization': 'torch CPU generator(seed) draws first97x256, second97x256, output256x97 standard normals. Slice width columns/rows. Embeddings multiply init_multiplier; projection multiply init_multiplier/sqrt(width); biases zero. Coupled directions across widths/arms. Norm arm globally rescales all parameters to same-seed width128 norm at selected multiplier.', 'arm_order': ['fixed_reference', 'candidate', 'zero_decay', 'initial_norm'], 'reference': {'learning_rate': 0.001, 'weight_decay': 1.0, 'init_multiplier': 1.0}, 'controls': ['constant', 'training_copy', 'initial_restore', 'input_shift'], 'control_expectations': 'Every candidate checkpoint uses same evaluation rows/count. Constant=lowest training-majority class. Copy=training lookup with majority fallback, equals exact fallback evaluation accuracy. Restore archived evaluator-owned initial state to scratch and require exact original logits. Input shift(a,b)->((a+1)%97,b) bijective/nonidentity/answer-changing and actual trained forward. If parent accuracy>=.95, diagnostic drop supported iff shift_accuracy<=.1 and drop>=.8; otherwise inconclusive. Mechanical validity, not desired outcome, gates eligibility. Identity/label-preserving/omitted controls invalid.', 'events': 'Step0 and every100 updates. Train>=.99, eval>=.95 sustained3 checkpoints; onset first of3. Grokking iff both observed and nonnegative delay>=1000 updates. Otherwise right censor. Restricted delay=1 if either onset missing, else max(0,generalization-fit)/horizon. Keep censor flags; cap is not observed time. Smoke checkpoints0..4 after4 updates cannot certify production.', 'aggregation': 'Equal checkpoints per arm, equal4 arms trajectory coverage; equal checkpoints and4 controls validity coverage. Episode=.5*trajectory+.25*controls+.25*candidate final accuracy. Seed-equal within width, width-equal. Balanced design equals fixed episode mean; smoke identity. Failed episode retains full weight score/accuracy/incidence/controls/completeness0, delay1. No dropping or renormalizing failures.', 'statistics': 'Seed-paired wide256-minus-narrow32 contrasts in normalized fit, generalization and restricted delay. Interactions subtract zero-decay and norm-arm width contrasts. Censored onset assigned horizon only for restricted comparisons with censor flags retained. Exact empirical paired seed-bootstrap enumeration with replacement and conservative floor/ceil percentile indices at .025/.975. Report all seed values and low resolution. No checkpoint/example pseudoreplication.', 'search_correct': 'All episodes/real arms/updates/controls complete, common allowed plan, finite trusted measurements, data/split integrity, exact transcript and budgets. No comparative, hypothesis sign, significance, novelty or grokking gate.', 'final_correct': 'All final episodes and baselines/controls complete with frozen source, allowed common plan, final integrity and exact budgets/transcript. Not hypothesis acceptance/publication. Cross-plane plan equivalence must additionally be audited from released evidence; no supported cross-plane configuration carrier exists for these self-contained evaluators.', 'rpc_operation_table': {'per_episode': {'reset': 1, 'plan': 1, 'training': 0, 'rollouts': 0, 'controls': 0, 'transfers': 0, 'replay': 0}, 'wire': 'No binary/state transfer allowed or needed, base64 bytes0; conservative protocol/id metadata+JSON+LF <16384 and strictly<67108864 bytes.'}, 'scheduling': 'Single monotonic deadline includes conservative startup; finish60s. Global reset5s+overhead16s reservations. Overhead sums four worker cleanups3s each+candidate cleanup3s+dispatch1s; TERM.5+KILL/reap.5+stderr<=.4 each. Equal per-method productive work allowance and later-arm reservations. Reference first exercises actual update/evaluation path. Preserve failures, continue resets/plans. No replay.', 'joint_budget': {'search': {'episode_count': 6, 'method_count': 4, 'wall_seconds': 14400, 'startup_seconds': 600, 'reset_seconds': 21, 'cleanup_seconds': 3, 'finish_seconds': 60, 'work_seconds': 480}, 'final': {'episode_count': 9, 'method_count': 4, 'wall_seconds': 43200, 'startup_seconds': 1200, 'reset_seconds': 21, 'cleanup_seconds': 3, 'finish_seconds': 60, 'work_seconds': 1080}}, 'limitations': ['Only addition p97, fixed architecture, limited seeds and finite horizons; no universal scaling or internal mechanism proof.', 'Scaffold is not the required paper. Publication needs latest official conference template, honest PDF/LaTeX/checklist/code and tables from actual task-run evidence.', 'Production throughput projected from reduced same-path calibration only, not full-horizon qualification.', 'Bounded hyperparameter controller only; no adaptive feedback, objectives, curricula or architecture API.', 'No research browsing during drafting; forbidden prior work not sought. Shared immutable code is not held-out data.']}, 'audit': {'cross_plane_content_disjoint': True, 'input_intersection_count': 0, 'example_intersection_count': 0, 'own_normalized_hash_set_sha256': '22c77f7eb0061422cc7eb4834b0eb50dc9ba04edb8e416d9b529c4f01681bbae', 'method': 'Privileged draft enumerated full source, hashed normalized raw inputs and examples before split, compared both sets ignoring IDs, checked provenance and per-seed split disjointness. Resource exposes only own pool and audit result.'}}\nsplits [('60613', {'train': 2823, 'evaluation': 1882, 'sha256': '5afe01b60f037b9311e3db9d9415737774d9c064d9727322517ffeec19ea491e'}), ('70717', {'train': 2823, 'evaluation': 1882, 'sha256': '502c9c9ecc85ba2411d1710178930eea798f17f6f61cdb659b26e63784dc9a16'}), ('80821', {'train': 2823, 'evaluation': 1882, 'sha256': '06f2f20a81c868dda306469edebc72686cee5f259c7e1edf94ede674e49e0022'})]\nallowlist known retrieval [('Power2022GrokkingGB', 'ref.s2.a1d1983a7b19845141e6505bd32dc395e5a136ba'), ('Liu2022OmnigrokGB', 'ref.s2.ad065eed8e1f727a8b0d8675802e4ffb1fcb87b4'), ('Kumar2023GrokkingAT', 'ref.s2.287839feb1e302fe513c2b03754ca44ad428634a'), ('Varma2023ExplainingGT', 'ref.s2.77b603850094ff749c9040772f8169a75145d506')]\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid public workload\")\n        checkpoints = request[\"checkpoints\"]\n        if (type(checkpoints) is not list or not checkpoints or checkpoints[0] != 0\n                or checkpoints[-1] != request[\"updates\"]\n                or any(type(step) is not int for step in checkpoints)\n                or checkpoints != sorted(set(checkpoints))):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid checkpoint schedule\")\n        _planned = True\n        return {\"learning_rate\": LEARNING_RATE, \"weight_decay\": WEIGHT_DECAY, \"init_multiplier\": INIT_MULTIPLIER}\n    raise ValueError(\"unsupported operation\")\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate that paper citations align with bibliography entries.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nSECTION_PATTERNS = {\n    \"abstract\": re.compile(\n        r\"\\\\begin\\{abstract\\}|\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*abstract[^}]*\\}\",\n        re.IGNORECASE,\n    ),\n    \"introduction\": re.compile(r\"\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*introduction[^}]*\\}\", re.IGNORECASE),\n    \"related work\": re.compile(r\"\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*related work[^}]*\\}\", re.IGNORECASE),\n    \"method\": re.compile(r\"\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*method[^}]*\\}\", re.IGNORECASE),\n    \"results\": re.compile(r\"\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*results[^}]*\\}\", re.IGNORECASE),\n    \"conclusion\": re.compile(r\"\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*conclusion[^}]*\\}\", re.IGNORECASE),\n    \"references\": re.compile(\n        r\"\\\\bibliography\\{|\\\\printbibliography|\\\\begin\\{thebibliography\\}|\\\\section\\*?\\{[^}]*references[^}]*\\}\",\n        re.IGNORECASE,\n    ),\n}\nCITE_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\cite[a-zA-Z*]*\\{([^}]+)\\}\")\nKEY_RE = re.compile(r\"@\\w+\\{([^,]+),\")\nSUPPLEMENT_HEADING_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\section\\s*\\{\\s*supplementary\\s+information\\s*\\}\",\n    re.IGNORECASE,\n)\nBIBLIOGRAPHY_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\bibliography\\s*\\{[^}]+\\}|\\\\printbibliography\\b(?:\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\"\n    r\"|\\\\begin\\s*\\{thebibliography\\}\",\n    re.IGNORECASE,\n)\nCLEARPAGE_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\clearpage\\b\", re.IGNORECASE)\nNEXT_SECTION_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\section\\*?\\s*(?:\\[[^\\[\\]]*\\]\\s*)?\\{\")\nLET_SECTION_ALIAS_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\let\\s*\\\\[a-zA-Z@]+\\s*=?\\s*\\\\section\\b\", re.IGNORECASE\n)\nNEWCOMMAND_DEFINITION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:newcommand|renewcommand)\\*?\\s*\\{\", re.IGNORECASE\n)\nDEF_DEFINITION_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:def|gdef|edef|xdef)\\s*\\\\[a-zA-Z@]+\", re.IGNORECASE\n)\nTEX_IMPORT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\(?:input|include)\\b\", re.IGNORECASE)\nSUBSTANTIVE_SUPPLEMENT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\subsection\\*?\\s*\\{|\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?:table|figure)\\*?\\}\",\n    re.IGNORECASE,\n)\nSUPPLEMENT_PLACEHOLDER_TEXTS = (\n    \"add supplementary material only when grounded artifacts support it\",\n    \"replace with grounded extended methods, reproducibility details, additional analyses, or supporting tables and figures\",\n)\nCONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\[a-zA-Z@]+\")\nNEWIF_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\newif\\s*(?P<name>\\\\if[a-zA-Z@]+)\")\nCONDITIONAL_OPENERS = frozenset(\n    {\n        r\"\\if\",\n        r\"\\ifcase\",\n        r\"\\ifcat\",\n        r\"\\ifcondition\",\n        r\"\\ifcsname\",\n        r\"\\ifdefined\",\n        r\"\\ifdim\",\n        r\"\\ifeof\",\n        r\"\\iffalse\",\n        r\"\\iffontchar\",\n        r\"\\ifhbox\",\n        r\"\\ifhmode\",\n        r\"\\ifincsname\",\n        r\"\\ifinner\",\n        r\"\\ifluatex\",\n        r\"\\ifmmode\",\n        r\"\\ifnum\",\n        r\"\\ifodd\",\n        r\"\\ifpdf\",\n        r\"\\ifpdfabsdim\",\n        r\"\\ifpdfabsnum\",\n        r\"\\ifpdfprimitive\",\n        r\"\\iftrue\",\n        r\"\\ifvbox\",\n        r\"\\ifvmode\",\n        r\"\\ifvoid\",\n        r\"\\ifx\",\n        r\"\\ifxetex\",\n    }\n)\nNON_CONDITIONAL_IF_MACROS = frozenset(\n    {\n        r\"\\ifblank\",\n        r\"\\ifbool\",\n        r\"\\ifboolexpr\",\n        r\"\\ifcsdef\",\n        r\"\\ifcsempty\",\n        r\"\\ifcsequal\",\n        r\"\\ifcsmacro\",\n        r\"\\ifcsparam\",\n        r\"\\ifcsprotected\",\n        r\"\\ifcsstring\",\n        r\"\\ifcsundef\",\n        r\"\\ifcsvoid\",\n        r\"\\ifdimcomp\",\n        r\"\\ifdimequal\",\n        r\"\\ifdimgreater\",\n        r\"\\ifdimless\",\n        r\"\\ifdef\",\n        r\"\\ifdefempty\",\n        r\"\\ifdefequal\",\n        r\"\\ifdefltxprotect\",\n        r\"\\ifdefmacro\",\n        r\"\\ifdefparam\",\n        r\"\\ifdefprotected\",\n        r\"\\ifdefstring\",\n        r\"\\ifdefvoid\",\n        r\"\\iflanguage\",\n        r\"\\ifltxcount\",\n        r\"\\ifltxcounter\",\n        r\"\\ifnumcomp\",\n        r\"\\ifnumequal\",\n        r\"\\ifnumgreater\",\n        r\"\\ifnumless\",\n        r\"\\ifstrequal\",\n        r\"\\ifstrempty\",\n        r\"\\ifthenelse\",\n        r\"\\iftoggle\",\n        r\"\\ifundef\",\n    }\n)\nVERBATIM_ENV_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?P<env>verbatim\\*?|lstlisting|minted)\\}.*?\"\n    r\"\\\\end\\s*\\{(?P=env)\\}\",\n    re.DOTALL,\n)\n\n\ndef parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n    \"\"\"Parse command-line arguments.\"\"\"\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Validate LaTeX sections and citation keys.\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--tex\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--bib\", required=True)\n    return parser.parse_args()\n\n\ndef _strip_tex_comments(tex_text: str) -> str:\n    cleaned_lines: list[str] = []\n    for line in tex_text.splitlines():\n        kept: list[str] = []\n        index = 0\n        while index < len(line):\n            character = line[index]\n            if line.startswith(r\"\\verb\", index):\n                delimiter_index = index + len(r\"\\verb\")\n                if delimiter_index < len(line) and line[delimiter_index] == \"*\":\n                    delimiter_index += 1\n                if (\n                    delimiter_index < len(line)\n                    and not line[delimiter_index].isspace()\n                    and not line[delimiter_index].isalpha()\n                ):\n                    closing_index = line.find(line[delimiter_index], delimiter_index + 1)\n                    if closing_index >= 0:\n                        kept.append(line[index : closing_index + 1])\n                        index = closing_index + 1\n                        continue\n            if character == \"%\" and not _is_escaped(line, index):\n                break\n            kept.append(character)\n            index += 1\n        cleaned_lines.append(\"\".join(kept))\n    return \"\\n\".join(cleaned_lines)\n\n\ndef _is_escaped(text: str, index: int) -> bool:\n    backslash_count = 0\n    cursor = index - 1\n    while cursor >= 0 and text[cursor] == \"\\\\\":\n        backslash_count += 1\n        cursor -= 1\n    return backslash_count % 2 == 1\n\n\ndef _strip_false_conditionals(\n    tex_text: str, conditional_openers: set[str] | None = None\n) -> str:\n    if conditional_openers is None:\n        conditional_openers = set(CONDITIONAL_OPENERS)\n        conditional_openers.update(\n            match.group(\"name\").lower() for match in NEWIF_RE.finditer(tex_text)\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated claim-grounding artifacts before paper finalization.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nKEY_RE = re.compile(r\"@\\w+\\{([^,]+),\")\nEVIDENCE_REF_RE = re.compile(r\"@evidence\\[\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\]\")\nTEX_INPUT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\\s*\"\n    r\"(?:\\{(?P<braced>[^{}]+)\\}|(?P<unbraced>[^\\s%{}]+))\"\n)\nTEX_IMPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?P<command>usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)\"\n    r\"(?![A-Za-z@])(?:\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\s*\\{(?P<targets>[^{}]+)\\}\"\n)\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)(?![A-Za-z@])\"\n)\nDYNAMIC_TEX_IMPORT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\csname\\s*(?:input|include)\\s*\\\\endcsname\")\nCONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\if[a-zA-Z@]+\\b|\\\\else\\b|\\\\fi\\b\")\nVERBATIM_ENV_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?P<env>verbatim\\*?|lstlisting|minted)\\}.*?\"\n    r\"\\\\end\\s*\\{(?P=env)\\}\",\n    re.DOTALL,\n)\nPROMPT_ARTIFACT_RE = re.compile(r\".+_prompt(?:_round_\\d+(?:_contract_retry_\\d+)?)?\\.md$\")\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\n    \"validation_feedback.json\",\n    \"validation_feedback.md\",\n    \"verification-report.json\",\n}\nROOT_GENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_NAMES = {\"validation_report.json\"}\nGENERATED_EVIDENCE_SCAN_ARTIFACT_PREFIXES = (\n    \"paper_evidence_audit\",\n)\nEVIDENCE_BUNDLE_DIRNAME = \"scientific-evidence\"\nEVIDENCE_SCAN_SUFFIXES = (\n    \".tex\",\n    \".md\",\n    \".json\",\n    \".yaml\",\n    \".yml\",\n    \".py\",\n    \".sh\",\n    \".r\",\n    \".csv\",\n    \".tsv\",\n)\nEVIDENCE_SKIP_DIR_NAMES = {\n    \".git\",\n    \"__pycache__\",\n    EVIDENCE_BUNDLE_DIRNAME,\n}\nAGENT_SKILL_DIR_PREFIXES = (\n    (\".claude\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".codex\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".cursor\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".opencode\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".gemini\", \"skills\"),\n    (\".pi\", \"agent\", \"skills\"),\n)\nVERIFICATION_SUMMARY_KEYS = (\n    \"total_references\",\n    \"resolved_references\",\n    \"anchored_references\",\n    \"dangling_references\",\n    \"manifests_checked\",\n)\nSCIENTIFIC_EVIDENCE_SCRIPT = (\n    Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\n    / \"scientific-evidence\"\n    / \"scripts\"\n    / \"scientific_evidence.py\"\n)\n\n\ndef read_json(path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Read JSON data from disk when available.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        payload = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Invalid JSON in {path}: {exc}\") from exc\n    if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n        raise SystemExit(f\"Expected JSON object in {path}\")\n    return payload\n\n\ndef read_bib_keys(path: Path) -> set[str]:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
